## DESCRIPTION
## Lagrange multipliers
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Lagrange multipliers')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "MathObjects.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

BEGIN_PGML


Find the maximum value of [` f(x,y,z) = x^2 - y^2 + z `] on the intersection of the surfaces [` x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 4 `] and [` x^2 - y^2 - z^2 = 1 `]. Use the method of Lagrange multipliers with many constraints.

[________]{Real(2.5+sqrt(3/2))}
END_PGML

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
BEGIN_SOLUTION
$PAR
You should find five solutions to the Lagrange system of equations resulting in a maximum value of \( \frac{5}{2} + \sqrt{\frac{3}{2}} \).
END_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();